  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer HfO2/SiO2 multilayer coating on fused silica substrate. Stack sequence: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | Fused Silica (12 bilayers, 24 finite layers total). Initialize HfO2 layers at 105 nm and SiO2 layers at 130 nm (quarter-wave at 450 nm center). Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with bounds: HfO2 80-200 nm, SiO2 100-180 nm. Evaluate coherent TMM at normal incidence across 300-450 nm (reflectance target) and 1000-1700 nm (transmittance target). Maximize mean reflectance in 300-450 nm band and mean transmittance in 1000-1700 nm band simultaneously. Outermost layer must be SiO2. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: low transmission in 300-450 nm; low reflection in 1000-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30; materials restricted to HfO2 and SiO2.",
